From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:55:45 +0000
Subject: Download filter lists from their publishers

Filter lists that cannot run page scripts are now downloaded from the
address their publisher gives, so they stay current. The two lists that
may run snippets, "ABP filters" and "Cromite experimental filters", are
still downloaded from the project site.

When a list that was never downloaded cannot be fetched, the retries
alternate between the publisher's address and a fallback: the copy on
the project site, or for HaGeZi lists the jsDelivr mirror their
publisher names. Installed lists stay in use when an update fails.

Settings offer 44 HaGeZi DNS blocklists in Adblock format. All are off
by default.

List downloads send no cookies and store none.

At startup, a subscription to the project site's copy of a list that its
publisher now serves moves to the publisher's address.

